# Voice adapter — PER-CLONE credential override. Copy to .env only if you need this clone to
# differ from the machine-global file; most setups need nothing here.
#
# Load order (scripts/voice/lib.sh):
#   1. ~/.config/aiworks/voice.env    mode 600, the real keys — the normal home for them
#   2. scripts/voice/.env             this file; a NON-EMPTY value overrides layer 1
#
# Why layer 1 exists at all: a Superset worktree gets STUB adapter .env files in this
# workspace (a known trap — the Jira/Slack creds are missing there), so a per-repo-only
# credential path would leave voice dead in every worktree. Keeping the real keys machine-
# global fixes that once. An EMPTY value here is ignored rather than treated as an override,
# so a stub cannot silently un-configure a working setup.
#
# ⚠ Never read, print, grep (without -q) or `bash -x` a real .env — see CLAUDE.md. A hook
#   (pretool-env-guard.sh) blocks it, but the rule is yours to keep.

# TTS + STT + sound effects. https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# STT (gpt-4o-transcribe) and the alternative TTS/summarizer. https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Deliberately NOT the image generator's GEMINI_API_KEY (decision #3): one key per feature
# keeps a voice quota problem out of the design pipeline. https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_VOICE_API_KEY=

# Optional TTS + STT alternative (sonic-3 / ink-whisper). https://play.cartesia.ai/keys
CARTESIA_API_KEY=
